From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 03:14:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 34/34] jsonrpc: reply count and reply-thread queries for reply
 threading

Add get_reply_count() and get_reply_thread() to src/message.rs plus thin
getMessageReplyCount/getMessageReplyThread JSON-RPC wrappers, for a
Telegram-style thread view in the web UI.

A reply is only counted when it is deliberate - it carries a quote and is
not forwarded - because mime_in_reply_to alone is set on every outgoing
message for email threading (prepare_msg_raw). Both stored forms of the
reply link are matched: the bare mid (outgoing) and the bracketed raw
In-Reply-To header (incoming). Threads are confined to one chat, so
"reply privately" answers stay out. get_reply_thread() walks quoted
parents up to the thread root (100-hop cycle cap) and collects the root
plus all nested replies with one recursive CTE, sorted by (timestamp, id).
Migration 155 adds an index on msgs.mime_in_reply_to to back the reverse
lookups.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
